    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG are delighted to bring Ballyfilibeen, Mourneabbey to the market for sale.\n\nOccupying a superb c. 7.5-acre site in a beautiful countryside setting, Ballyfilibeen offers a rare opportunity to acquire a substantial detached bungalow with generous living accommodation, extensive outdoor space and enormous potential.\n\nApproached via a long private driveway, the property enjoys a wonderful sense of privacy and seclusion while remaining within easy commuting distance of Cork City, Mallow and surrounding towns. Set amongst the rolling countryside of Mourneabbey, the location offers the perfect opportunity for those seeking a peaceful rural lifestyle without being too far removed from everyday amenities and transport links.\n\nThe detached bungalow, which extends to approximately 135 sq. m., provides well-proportioned accommodation throughout and would make an ideal family home. While the property is in need of modernisation, the generous accommodation and excellent site provide a superb blank canvas for a purchaser to create a home tailored to their own requirements and taste.\n\nThe accommodation briefly comprises:\n\nLiving Room: 4.1m x 3.8m laminate flooring.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room: 5.2m x 5.1m fully fitted kitchen with glass sliding doors providing access to the garden.\n\nLiving Room: 3.1m x 5.2m laminate flooring, stove and double doors leading to the kitchen/dining room.\n\nUtility Room: 3.7m x 2.1m with back door.\n\nToilet: 1.9m x 1.6m tiled, with electric shower.\n\nBedroom 1: 3.6m x 3.1m carpet flooring.\n\nBedroom 2: 2.7m x 3.1m laminate flooring.\n\nBedroom 3: 4.4m x 3.1m carpet flooring.\n\nBathroom: 3.1m x 1.9m with bath.\n\nBedroom 4: 3.1m x 3.1m laminate flooring.\n\nExternally, the property really comes into its own. The substantial c. 7.5-acre holding provides an abundance of space and offers considerable scope for a variety of uses, subject to the necessary planning requirements. The extensive grounds could appeal to those with equestrian interests, hobby farming aspirations or simply a desire for additional land, privacy and outdoor space.\n\nA generous yard area is complemented by a selection of sheds and outhouses, providing valuable storage and workshop space and offering further potential for a range of uses. The combination of the house, outbuildings, yard and extensive lands makes this a particularly versatile property.\n\nBallyfilibeen represents an exciting opportunity for purchasers with vision. Whether modernised and transformed into a contemporary family home or developed to suit individual requirements, the property offers the space, privacy and setting from which to create something truly special.\n\nKEY FEATURES:\n\nSubstantial 4-bedroom, 2-bathroom detached bungalow\nExtending to approximately 135 sq. m.\nSet on a generous c. 7.5-acre site\nBuilt c. 1975\nBeautiful and peaceful countryside setting\nLong private driveway approaching the residence\nGenerous yard area\nSelection of sheds and outhouses\nExcellent potential for modernisation and upgrading\nSpacious and well-proportioned living accommodation\nOil-fired central heating\nSeptic tank\nWell water\nIdeal for those seeking space, privacy and a rural lifestyle\nPotential for equestrian, hobby farming or outdoor pursuits, subject to planning\nConvenient location within easy commuting distance of Cork City and Mallow\nA rare opportunity to create a wonderful family home on an impressive landholding\n\nBallyfilibeen is a property with genuine potential, offering an exceptional combination of accommodation, extensive lands, privacy and a superb rural setting. Early viewing is highly recommended to fully appreciate what this property has to offer\n\nThese particulars are for information only and are given under the strict understanding that they do not form part of any contract. Neither whole nor any part of this document or any reference thereto may be included in any public document, circular or statement nor published without the written consent of DNG John Ryan. PSL: 003615"
      },
